<article class="env-lemma" id="00O9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00O9">Lemma <span data-tag="00O9">10.110.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $n \geq 0$ be an integer. Then $R$ has finite global dimension $\leq n$ if and only if for all maximal ideals $\mathfrak m$ of $R$ the ring $R_{\mathfrak m}$ has global dimension $\leq n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We saw, Lemma <a href="/tag/00O8" data-tag="00O8">10.109.13</a> that if $R$ has finite global dimension $n$, then all the localizations $R_{\mathfrak m}$ have finite global dimension at most $n$. Conversely, suppose that all the $R_{\mathfrak m}$ have global dimension $\leq n$. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. Let $0 \to K_ n \to F_{n-1} \to \ldots \to F_0 \to M \to 0$ be a resolution with $F_ i$ finite free. Then $K_ n$ is a finite $R$-module. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/00O5" data-tag="00O5">10.109.3</a> and the assumption all the modules $K_ n \otimes _ R R_{\mathfrak m}$ are projective. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a> the module $K_ n$ is finite projective. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>